WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
We talk a lot about origin stories here, how one idea can change everything.
我们经常在这里讨论起源故事，以及一个想法如何能改变一切。

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.440
Well, the team at Puck News just launched a fantastic new podcast series
Puck News 的团队刚刚推出了一档精彩绝伦的全新播客系列

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.960
that takes that concept to a whole new level.
将这个概念提升到了一个全新的高度。

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.000
It's called The Making of a President.
它叫做《总统是如何炼成的》（The Making of a President）。

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.280
It's hosted by veteran political reporter Peter Hamby.
由资深政治记者彼得·汉比（Peter Hamby）主持。

6
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.320
The series takes you straight into the war rooms of modern political campaigns.
这个系列将带你直击现代政治竞选的战情室。

7
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.040
It pulls back the curtain on high-stakes decisions,
为你揭开高风险决策的神秘面纱，

8
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.480
hidden mechanics, and key operatives shaping our nation's leadership.
探寻塑造我们国家领导层的隐藏机制和关键操盘手。

9
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.680
And whether you're a political junkie, and by the way, I am a political junkie.
无论你是不是政治迷，顺便说一句，我就是一个政治迷。

10
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.320
I have started listening to this podcast, and it is incredible.
我一直在听这个播客，简直太棒了。

11
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.100
The level of detail that Peter goes into with his guests.
彼得与他的嘉宾们探讨的细节深度惊人。

12
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.300
This is not just a quickie interview like you get on most news shows.
这可不是你在大多数新闻节目中看到的那种草草了事的采访。

13
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.220
This is a true deep dive.
这是一次真正深度挖掘。

14
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.140
But whether you're a political junkie or just love any high-stakes human drama,
但无论你是政治迷，还是单纯喜欢惊心动魄的人性戏剧，

15
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.860
The Making of a President offers an incredible look at how power is actually won.
《总统是如何炼成的》都将为你呈现权力是如何被真正赢得的精彩视角。

16
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.840
Here now is a quick preview of episode one.
以下是第一集的精彩片段预告。

17
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.040
Make sure to search The Making of a President wherever you listen and subscribe today.
请在各大播客平台搜索《总统是如何炼成的》并立即订阅。

18
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.300
We've also put a link to the show in this episode description.
我们还在本集的简介中附上了该节目的链接。

19
00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:21.090
Welcome, everybody, to my brand-new show for Puck about the 2028 campaign,
欢迎大家来到我为 Puck 主持的关于 2028 年大选的全新节目，

20
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.530
The Making of a President.
《总统是如何炼成的》。

21
00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.670
Thank you so much for joining me.
非常感谢大家的收听。

22
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.830
And since this is the first episode, before getting into my feisty interview today with Rahm Emanuel,
既然这是第一集，在开始我今天与拉姆·伊曼纽尔（Rahm Emanuel）的精彩访谈之前，

23
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.110
I wanted to put on the table what this show is and what it is not.
我想先明确一下这个节目是什么，以及它不是什么。

24
00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.790
We are in a midterm election right now, I know,
我知道我们现在正处于中期选举期间，

25
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.070
but the presidential campaign jockeying is already underway behind the scenes,
但总统竞选的暗中角力已经在幕后展开，

26
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.310
and it will kick off for real immediately after the midterms conclude in November.
并且将在 11 月中期选举结束后立即正式拉开帷幕。

27
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:50.470
I want this show to be about how politics and campaigns really work.
我希望这个节目能展现政治和竞选的真实运作方式。

28
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.850
As much as I'm a political junkie, and this will be my sixth presidential campaign,
尽管我是一个政治迷，而且这也将是我报道的第六场总统大选，

29
00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.570
it's long been a gripe of mine that political journalism is kind of a cocoon.
但我一直有个抱怨，那就是政治新闻有些像是作茧自缚。

30
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.310
A bunch of operatives and journalists talking to each other without pausing
一堆操盘手和记者自说自话，却从不停下来

31
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.230
to explain to viewers and voters what exactly they're talking about.
向观众和选民解释他们到底在谈论什么。

32
00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.590
Our conversations on this podcast are going to be smart and elevated,
我们在本播客中的对话将既聪明又高端，

33
00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:15.210
but we're going to focus on the business of presidential campaigns.
但我们将专注于总统竞选的商业本质。

34
00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.650
And the gears that move them from the inside.
以及从内部推动它们的齿轮。

35
00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.210
How messages and memes get pushed out.
信息和模因（meme）是如何被推送到大众面前的。

36
00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.330
How the money works.
资金是如何运作的。

37
00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.630
How do you win a specific primary state?
你该如何在某个特定的初选州获胜？

38
00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.390
Why does that state matter more than another state?
为什么这个州比其他州更重要？

39
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.250
Does polling even work anymore?
民调现在到底还管不管用？

40
00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.910
This won't be a show reacting to every micro news cycle or Trump headline.
这个节目不会去回应每一个微观新闻周期或特朗普的头条新闻。

41
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.190
There are too many options out there on that front.
在这方面，外界已经有太多的选择了。

42
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.370
We'll obviously talk about the news and issues and big names.
我们当然会讨论新闻、议题和重要人物。

43
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.890
Those things define the rhythms of any campaign.
这些东西决定了一场竞选的节奏。

44
00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.450
But we won't live and die by the news cycle.
但我们不会被新闻周期所左右。

45
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.410
Instead, I want to bring you conversations with the players who call the shots.
相反，我希望带你聆听那些运筹帷幄的决策者的访谈。

46
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:52.930
People who can explain trends in media and technology and demographics.
他们能够解释媒体、技术和人口统计数据的趋势。

47
00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.490
And the campaign operatives who are grappling with the fact that the rules of modern campaigning,
还有那些正在极力应对现实的竞选操盘手，他们发现我们本以为早已了然的现代竞选规则，

48
00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.390
we all thought we knew, are being broken and rewritten in real time.
正在被实时打破和重写。

49
00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:09.890
The 2028 campaign will be the most unpredictable, unmediated, and wide-open presidential race we've ever seen.
2028 年的竞选将是我们见过的最不可预测、最没有中间环节、最开放的总统大选。

50
00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.530
We're going to talk to Republicans and Democrats.
我们将与共和党人和民主党人展开对话。

51
00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:16.470
And while we have a likely 2028 contender on the show today,
虽然我们今天节目请到了一位2028年大选的潜在竞争者，

52
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:19.210
we won't always interview candidates and politicians.
但我们并不总是只采访候选人和政治家。

53
00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.350
The decision makers and hustlers behind the scenes are just as interesting.
幕后的决策者和推手同样引人入胜。

54
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:26.410
I know way too many of them at this point in my career,
在我职业生涯的这个阶段，我认识的这类人实在是太多了，

55
00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:31.450
and I want to do my best as we like to do at Puck to make those private conversations public
正如我们在Puck一贯的做法，我想尽最大努力将这些私下对话公之于众，

56
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.670
and help all of us make sense of the carnival ride we're about to go on.
并帮助大家看清我们即将经历的这场狂欢般的政治大戏。

57
00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.870
If you're into all that, make sure you subscribe.
如果你对这些感兴趣，请务必订阅。

58
00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.630
My guest today is Rahm Emanuel.
我今天的嘉宾是伊曼纽尔。

59
00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.370
If you know politics, you know...
如果你了解政治，你就知道……

60
00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.930
We hope you enjoyed that preview.
希望你喜欢刚才的预览。

61
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.590
To listen to the full episode, search for The Making of a President.
想要收听完整单集，请搜索《总统是如何炼成的》。

62
00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.330
Available everywhere you get your podcasts.
各大播客平台均可收听。

63
00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:53.670
We'll see you next time.
我们下期再见。
